# UMSH coloring rules — import from Wireshark's View → Coloring Rules → Import,
# or run `make install-colorfilters` to prepend this to the personal rule set.
#
# A Lua dissector cannot color a packet-list row; only a coloring rule can.
# The dissector puts the text of each prohibition it finds in a `umsh.violation`
# field for exactly this rule to match on.
#
# Rules are evaluated top to bottom and the first match wins, so this has to sit
# above the generic transport rules (UDP in particular) to reach a UMSH frame
# carried over the synthetic capture encapsulation.
@UMSH Protocol Violation@umsh.violation@[65535,0,0][65535,65535,65535]
